    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int 5{e}^{4x}{({e}^{4x}+4)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{4x}+4.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{5}{4}\\text{d}u=5{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{e}^{4x}{({e}^{4x}+4)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {({e}^{4x}+4)}^{3}\\cdot 5{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\frac{5}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{({e}^{4x}+4)}^{4}}{16}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
