    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{6^{x + 1}}{\\sqrt{6^{x} + 3}}dx$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=6^{x} + 3.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6^{x}\\ln 6\\,⟹\\,\\frac{6}{\\ln 6}\\,\\text{d}u=6^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{6^{x+1}}{\\sqrt{6^{x} + 3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot\\frac{6}{\\ln 6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{\\ln 6}\\int u^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{12\\sqrt{u}}{\\ln 6}+C \\\\ & =\\frac{12\\sqrt{6^{x} + 3}}{\\ln 6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
